  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Grouped Standard",
    "overview": "Vector plays the category standard straight. It is built the way Apple Health and Fitness, Strong, MacroFactor and Whoop are built: a grey grouped ground, white cells floating on it by tone alone, one green tint that means \"you can act here\", and a fixed colour per area so the header of a cell tells you where you are before you read it. Nothing is invented for its own sake. The craft is in doing the native thing exactly: continuous corners, Dynamic Type everywhere, big rounded numerals, sentence-case labels, and one decision on screen at a time.\n\nThe density is comfortable rather than packed. Today is a single column of cells separated by a 36 pt section rhythm on a 16 pt gutter; each cell opens with a tinted category header, states one thing in a bold title, backs it with numbers in SF Pro Rounded, and offers at most one filled action. Dark mode is designed, not inverted: a pure black ground with #1C1C1E cells and a brighter green that carries black text.\n\nThe system refuses the gamified (achievement badges, confetti, neon), the clinical (spreadsheet coldness) and the \"bro\" register (aggressive black-and-red). Recommendations come from rules, so they are marked with a scope, never a sparkle.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Grey grouped ground, white cells, no strokes or shadows on content.",
      "One green tint for actions, selection, links and the tab bar.",
      "Category colour lives in the cell's header: Coach and Training green, Nutrition orange, Body indigo.",
      "Macros are a fixed categorical set: protein blue, carbs teal, fat amber, calories orange.",
      "SF Pro for words, SF Pro Rounded bold with tabular figures for numbers.",
      "Sentence case everywhere; no eyebrows, no tracked uppercase labels.",
      "One filled primary per view; secondary actions are tinted, not filled."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Tint Rule",
        "body": "Green is the only colour that means \"act\". If something is tappable and filled, it is Action Green; nothing else gets a filled button.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Header Carries the Category Rule",
        "body": "Category colour appears in a cell's `CategoryHeader` symbol and label (and in matching row icons), never as a cell fill, border or background wash.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Never Colour Alone Rule",
        "body": "Status and macro colours are always paired with an icon, sign or label.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Every label, header, button and title is sentence case. No uppercase, no letter-spacing, no small label above a heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rounded Numbers Rule",
        "body": "A number the user is meant to read as a result is SF Pro Rounded bold with tabular figures and animates with a numeric content transition. Words never use the rounded face.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dynamic Type Rule",
        "body": "Sizes above are the default Large setting; every style scales. `minimumScaleFactor` is allowed only on single-line metrics.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Decision Rule",
        "body": "A cell states one thing and offers one way forward. The Weekly Check-In leads with the decision, then the week; evidence sits behind \"Why?\" rather than on the surface.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Cell Rule",
        "body": "A content cell never casts a shadow or carries a border. If a surface needs a shadow, it must be floating over scrolling content on material.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** put every piece of content in a 14 pt Cell White cell on the grouped ground, padded 16 pt, separated by 36 pt.",
      "**Do** open a cell with a `CategoryHeader` in its category colour: Coach and Training green, Nutrition orange, Body indigo.",
      "**Do** keep to one filled Action Green button per view; make companions secondary (Green Wash) or inline text.",
      "**Do** set result numbers in SF Pro Rounded bold with tabular figures, and pair every status or macro colour with an icon, sign or label.",
      "**Do** use `AdaptiveStack` for paired buttons so they stack at large text sizes.",
      "**Do** press down on the 0.1 s ease-out and release on the 0.28 s snappy curve; collapse motion to a 0.15 s fade under Reduce Motion.",
      "**Do** keep bounce for rare moments (a PR, workout complete); completing a set stays crisp."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** give content cells shadows, strokes or category-coloured fills.",
      "**Don't** use uppercase, letter-spacing or a small label above a heading (no eyebrows or kickers).",
      "**Don't** use a sparkle or magic glyph for recommendations; use `scope`.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second action colour or fill a button in a category colour.",
      "**Don't** add achievement badges, confetti, streak pressure or neon; don't use aggressive black-and-red.",
      "**Don't** use emoji; SF Symbols only."
    ]
  }
